GNU datetime NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

* Version 2.0.20260915181840 (2026-09-15)

** Release: cross-platform binaries + shell integrations

   Binaries for linux-amd64, linux-arm64, windows-amd64,
   windows-arm64, macos-intel, macos-arm are in
   dist/datetime-2.0.20260915181840-*.tar.gz (source is
   dist/datetime-2.0.20260915181840.tar.gz). Each bundles datetime +
   timestamp plus bash/zsh/fish completions.
   `make check` passed (full test gate) before tagging.

** Shell integration

   New zsh (shell/datetime.zsh + shell/timestamp.zsh) and fish
   (shell/datetime.fish + shell/timestamp.fish) completions,
   parity with bash. `make install` deploys to
   $(zshdir) and $(fishdir); `make dist` packs them.

** Build and release

   `make release` (this release) bumps __version__ via
   ~/sbin/timestamp, regenerates docs (man/tldr/README), runs
   the full test battery, cross-builds 6 platform binaries into
   dist/release/, and creates per-platform tarballs in dist/.
   `make dist` writes to dist/datetime-$(VERSION).tar.gz.


